{"event_type":"review","id":"c8825be03736f679b76642348ac055927f388f17e3976fef51ff6be6bffe32a6","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T06:47:45Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/94f9007626e82b570285e82658b54309d7bd6d98a4c3d5916c765d8976ac0d02","sha256":"94f9007626e82b570285e82658b54309d7bd6d98a4c3d5916c765d8976ac0d02"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/21c285d409d4546191d11d8eb6cd84f54f0bb5c6007246bd74209afdd312d10a","sha256":"21c285d409d4546191d11d8eb6cd84f54f0bb5c6007246bd74209afdd312d10a"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d50cc521f377783d61e4406011f95408e694ad0bcae47b64ead49270a576c134","sha256":"d50cc521f377783d61e4406011f95408e694ad0bcae47b64ead49270a576c134"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b4a9a18391d4906cec5a5123adc6c2700645d74321244380786fc4456fcbda25","sha256":"b4a9a18391d4906cec5a5123adc6c2700645d74321244380786fc4456fcbda25"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6bd1b04addfe1b2f680731bc365b48437e5c1a99bb7d8a103313a25fb4af8300","sha256":"6bd1b04addfe1b2f680731bc365b48437e5c1a99bb7d8a103313a25fb4af8300"}],"attempt_id":"83c5e7a383d941f56a8fcdb595cb9f35e6f7748217273cfcfe83ad1f6ad35e0a:0:1","base":"9f137309c5ebdfb45056279b8ae57ecb7960bf17","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"588f88e435f35090f77af1312c5a419d48af6959","body":"**`update()` resets already-sent outbox rows to `pending`, so a repeated destination re-sends completed notifications.**\n\nThe outbox key is `ledger.digest([request_id, event_id, accepted])`. It is deterministic for a given destination. Line 47 assigns a new `dict(... state=\"pending\")` unconditionally. Calling `update()` again with the same destination, for example a client retry of `notify-update`, overwrites any `sent` row for that key. This also discards `attempts` and `next_at`. The next `drain` then sends the same completion message again.\n\nAt-least-once delivery covers crashes. It does not cover an idempotent re-submit of an unchanged destination.\n\nKeep `sent` rows. Re-arm only `withdrawn` and `error` rows, which is what a destination replace or restore needs. No test covers `update()` called twice with the same destination after a successful drain.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                key = ledger.digest([request_id, event_id, accepted])\n-                q.setdefault(\"review_notify_outbox\", {})[key] = dict(v=1, request_id=request_id,\n-                    event_id=event_id, destination=accepted, state=\"pending\", receipt_id=event[\"receipt_id\"])\n+                key = ledger.digest([request_id, event_id, accepted])\n+                outbox = q.setdefault(\"review_notify_outbox\", {})\n+                if outbox.get(key, {}).get(\"state\") == \"sent\":\n+                    continue\n+                outbox[key] = dict(v=1, request_id=request_id,\n+                    event_id=event_id, destination=accepted, state=\"pending\", receipt_id=event[\"receipt_id\"])\n```\n</details>","id":"a5ab263f4be90d73a4c9aff4d63acc4614f37ea21db2ee86d59c0dd6922d1d90","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_notify.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`update()` resets already-sent outbox rows to `pending`, so a repeated destination re-sends completed notifications."}],"head":"a2c37e2453f98cc5c61605fc99cefab026c8dc0e","head_tree":"1393f525755319d0614b0af7f33278d124294c49","input_scope":[{"blob":"ce57ea5016e6d6a0ab4b23ce6c869b46d23bb53d","intervals":[[1,127]],"path":"apps/crq-python/local_review_pr.py"},{"blob":"588f88e435f35090f77af1312c5a419d48af6959","intervals":[[1,107]],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_notify.py"},{"blob":"e74cec6ed6a2d584f2e3df3de909519789755bd9","intervals":[[1,50]],"path":"apps/crq-python/re